  {
   "path": "SCENE.md",
   "role": "instructions",
   "content": "# Halftone Print\n\nA scene printed instead of displayed: cyan, magenta and yellow dot screens at their own angles on warm paper, each plate a touch out of register. Runs its WebGL shader over its own built-in scene (a paper poster; kicker, headline and paragraph from variables), not over the host video. Best on light, graphic scenes with real midtones.\n\nCategory: filters. Length: 3.0 s. WebGL: yes.\n\nUse when:\n- A scene should read as printed rather than displayed: zine intros, riso posters, editorial title cards.\n- The scene is light and graphic with real midtones, which is where a dot screen has something to render.\n\nAvoid when:\n- Only one element should feel papery while the rest stays clean: use paper-sticker or paper-wobble.\n- The scene is dark: nearly every cell saturates to full ink and the screen disappears into a solid field.\n- Small type has to stay readable: a dot screen keeps only a cell's colour.\n\nVariables:\n- kicker (string): Kicker, default \"Issue 04\"\n- headline (string): Headline, default \"Ship the demo, not the deck\"\n- body (string): Body, default \"A recorded product beats a rehearsed one. Cut it in the afternoon and send it before the meeting.\"\n- dot_size (number, 4-32): Dot size, default 10\n- angle (number, 0-90): Angle, default 0\n- misregistration (number, 0-6): Misregistration, default 1.2\n- paper_tint (color): Paper, default \"#f4efe4\"\n- resolution (number, 0.25-1): Resolution, default 1\n\nSource: https://github.com/Remocn/remocn. Licence: MIT. The scene file keeps the upstream notice.\n"
  },
  {
   "path": "scene.html",
   "role": "source",
   "content": "<!doctype html>\n<!--\n  Halftone Print\n\n  A scene printed onto paper: rotated dot screens per ink colour, slightly out of register.\n  The scene here is a paper poster.\n\n  Ported to an HTML + GSAP sub-composition by usemosio/blocks from:\n  https://github.com/Remocn/remocn/blob/126221ae00ba86eb40b65731b125ff398687d3b7/registry/remocn/halftone-print/index.tsx\n\n  MIT License\n\n  Copyright (c) 2026 Remocn\n\n  Permission is hereby granted, free of charge, to any person obtaining a copy\n  of this software and associated documentation files (the \"Software\"), to deal\n  in the Software without restriction, including without limitation the rights\n  to use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute, sublicense, and/or sell\n  copies of the Software, and to permit persons to whom the Software is\n  furnished to do so, subject to the following conditions:\n\n  The above copyright notice and this permission notice shall be included in all\n  copies or substantial portions of the Software.\n\n  THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED \"AS IS\", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR\n  IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY,\n  FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE\n  AUTHORS OR COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER\n  LIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM,\n  OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE OR THE USE OR OTHER DEALINGS IN THE\n  SOFTWARE.\n\n  remocn captures its React children with the HTML-in-Canvas API, which a render machine does\n  not have. This block draws remocn's preview scene (a paper poster) (text and colours from the variables) on a\n  2D canvas and runs remocn's fragment shader over it, so it applies the look to its own content,\n  not to the host video behind it.\n-->\n<html\n  lang=\"en\"\n  data-composition-id=\"halftone-print\"\n  data-composition-duration=\"3\"\n  data-composition-variables='[{\"id\": \"kicker\", \"type\": \"string\", \"role\": \"content\", \"label\": \"Kicker\", \"description\": \"Small line above the headline in the sample poster.\", \"default\": \"Issue 04\"}, {\"id\": \"headline\", \"type\": \"string\", \"role\": \"content\", \"label\": \"Headline\", \"description\": \"Headline of the sample poster.\", \"default\": \"Ship the demo, not the deck\"}, {\"id\": \"body\", \"type\": \"string\", \"role\": \"content\", \"label\": \"Body\", \"description\": \"Paragraph under the headline.\", \"default\": \"A recorded product beats a rehearsed one. Cut it in the afternoon and send it before the meeting.\"}, {\"id\": \"dot_size\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Dot size\", \"description\": \"Spacing of the dot screen. Pixel sizes are for a 1280×720 frame and scale with the frame.\", \"default\": 10, \"min\": 4, \"max\": 32, \"step\": 1, \"unit\": \"px\"}, {\"id\": \"angle\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Angle\", \"description\": \"Rotation of the whole screen set.\", \"default\": 0, \"min\": 0, \"max\": 90, \"step\": 1, \"unit\": \"deg\"}, {\"id\": \"misregistration\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Misregistration\", \"description\": \"How far the plates sit out of register. Pixel sizes are for a 1280×720 frame and scale with the frame.\", \"default\": 1.2, \"min\": 0, \"max\": 6, \"step\": 0.2, \"unit\": \"px\"}, {\"id\": \"paper_tint\", \"type\": \"color\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Paper\", \"description\": \"Colour of the paper.\", \"default\": \"#f4efe4\"}, {\"id\": \"resolution\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"quality\", \"label\": \"Resolution\", \"description\": \"Share of the frame size the shader is drawn at, then scaled up. Fine dots need 1; lower renders faster but the screen turns soft.\", \"default\": 1, \"min\": 0.25, \"max\": 1, \"step\": 0.05}]'\n>\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\" />\n    <title>Halftone Print</title>\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <template>\n      <link\n        rel=\"stylesheet\"\n        href=\"https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Geist:wght@400;500;600&amp;family=Geist+Mono:wght@400&amp;display=block\"\n      />\n      <style>\n        #root {\n          position: absolute;\n          inset: 0;\n          overflow: hidden;\n          container-type: size;\n          background: #000;\n          pointer-events: none;\n        }\n        .htp-stage {\n          position: absolute;\n          inset: 0;\n        }\n        .htp-canvas,\n        .htp-scene {\n          position: absolute;\n          inset: 0;\n          width: 100%;\n          height: 100%;\n          display: block;\n        }\n        .htp-scene {\n          display: none;\n        }\n        .htp-off .htp-canvas {\n          display: none;\n        }\n        .htp-off .htp-fb {\n          display: block;\n        }\n      </style>\n\n      <div id=\"root\" data-composition-id=\"halftone-print\" data-duration=\"3\" data-fps=\"30\">\n        <div id=\"htp-clip\" class=\"htp-stage clip\" data-start=\"0\" data-duration=\"3\" data-track-index=\"0\">\n          <canvas id=\"htp-scene0\" class=\"htp-scene htp-fb\"></canvas>\n          <canvas id=\"htp-canvas\" class=\"htp-canvas\"></canvas>\n        </div>\n\n        <script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/gsap@3.14.2/dist/gsap.min.js\"></script>\n        <script>\n          (function () {\n            \"use strict\";\n            var NAME = \"halftone-print\";\n            var root = document.getElementById(\"root\");\n            var stage = document.getElementById(\"htp-clip\");\n            var canvas = document.getElementById(\"htp-canvas\");\n            var vars =\n              window.__hyperframes && window.__hyperframes.getVariables\n                ? window.__hyperframes.getVariables()\n                : {};\n            function clampNum(value, fallback, min, max) {\n              var n = Number(value);\n              return Number.isFinite(n) ? Math.min(max, Math.max(min, n)) : fallback;\n            }\n            function hex(value, fallback) {\n              var m = /^#?([0-9a-f]{3}|[0-9a-f]{6})$/i.exec(String(value || \"\").trim());\n              if (!m) return fallback;\n              var h = m[1].length === 3 ? m[1].replace(/./g, \"$&$&\") : m[1];\n              return \"#\" + h.toLowerCase();\n            }\n            function rgb(value) {\n              var h = hex(value, \"#ffffff\").slice(1);\n              return [parseInt(h.slice(0, 2), 16) / 255, parseInt(h.slice(2, 4), 16) / 255, parseInt(h.slice(4, 6), 16) / 255];\n            }\n            var DEFS = [{\"id\": \"kicker\", \"type\": \"string\", \"default\": \"Issue 04\"}, {\"id\": \"headline\", \"type\": \"string\", \"default\": \"Ship the demo, not the deck\"}, {\"id\": \"body\", \"type\": \"string\", \"default\": \"A recorded product beats a rehearsed one. Cut it in the afternoon and send it before the meeting.\"}, {\"id\": \"dot_size\", \"type\": \"number\", \"default\": 10, \"min\": 4, \"max\": 32}, {\"id\": \"angle\", \"type\": \"number\", \"default\": 0, \"min\": 0, \"max\": 90}, {\"id\": \"misregistration\", \"type\": \"number\", \"default\": 1.2, \"min\": 0, \"max\": 6}, {\"id\": \"paper_tint\", \"type\": \"color\", \"default\": \"#f4efe4\"}, {\"id\": \"resolution\", \"type\": \"number\", \"default\": 1, \"min\": 0.25, \"max\": 1}];\n            var V = {};\n            DEFS.forEach(function (d) {\n              var raw = vars[d.id];\n              if (d.type === \"number\") V[d.id] = clampNum(raw, d.default, d.min, d.max);\n              else if (d.type === \"color\") V[d.id] = hex(raw, d.default);\n              else if (d.type === \"boolean\") V[d.id] = typeof raw === \"boolean\" ? raw : raw === \"true\" ? true : raw === \"false\" ? false : d.default;\n              else if (d.type === \"enum\") V[d.id] = d.options.indexOf(raw) >= 0 ? raw : d.default;\n              else V[d.id] = typeof raw === \"string\" && raw.trim() ? raw.trim() : d.default;\n            });\n\n            var W = Math.max(2, root.clientWidth);\n            var H = Math.max(2, root.clientHeight);\n            var res = V.resolution;\n            var cw = Math.max(2, Math.round(W * res));\n            var ch = Math.max(2, Math.round(H * res));\n            var sceneCanvases = [\"htp-scene0\"].map(function (id) {\n              var el = document.getElementById(id);\n              el.width = cw;\n              el.height = ch;\n              return el;\n            });\n\n            var SANS = \"Geist, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, sans-serif\";\n            var MONO = \"'Geist Mono', ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace\";\n            var INK = \"#f2f2f2\";\n            var MUTED = \"#8b8f9a\";\n            var TONES = [\"#a1eebd\", \"#ffb38e\", \"#d4b3ff\"];\n            var S = Math.min(W / 940, H / 720);\n            function setFont(ctx, weight, size, family) { ctx.font = weight + \" \" + size + \"px \" + family; }\n            function fitFont(ctx, text, maxWidth, weight, size, family) {\n              setFont(ctx, weight, size, family);\n              var w = ctx.measureText(text).width;\n              if (w > maxWidth) { size *= maxWidth / w; setFont(ctx, weight, size, family); }\n              return size;\n            }\n            function setSpacing(ctx, px) { if (\"letterSpacing\" in ctx) ctx.letterSpacing = px + \"px\"; }\n            function wrapLines(ctx, text, maxWidth) {\n              var words = String(text).split(/\\s+/).filter(Boolean);\n              var lines = [];\n              var line = \"\";\n              words.forEach(function (word) {\n                var next = line ? line + \" \" + word : word;\n                if (line && ctx.measureText(next).width > maxWidth) { lines.push(line); line = word; }\n                else line = next;\n              });\n              if (line) lines.push(line);\n              return lines;\n            }\n            function pairs(text, max) {\n              return String(text).split(\";\")\n                .map(function (row) { return row.split(\"|\").map(function (part) { return part.trim(); }); })\n                .filter(function (row) { return row[0]; })\n                .slice(0, max);\n            }\n            function begin(ctx, cw, ch, fill) {\n              ctx.setTransform(cw / W, 0, 0, ch / H, 0, 0);\n              ctx.fillStyle = fill;\n              ctx.fillRect(0, 0, W, H);\n              ctx.textBaseline = \"middle\";\n              ctx.textAlign = \"left\";\n              setSpacing(ctx, 0);\n            }\n\n\n            // Sample scene \"poster\": a paper poster with a headline and three colour bars (remocn's CanvasScenePoster).\n            function drawPoster(canvas) {\n              var ctx = canvas.getContext(\"2d\");\n              begin(ctx, canvas.width, canvas.height, \"#efe9dc\");\n              var s = S, pad, inner, headLines, bodyLines, total;\n              var headSize, bodySize;\n              for (var attempt = 0; attempt < 3; attempt++) {\n                pad = 96 * s; inner = W - pad * 2;\n                headSize = 92 * s; bodySize = 32 * s;\n                setFont(ctx, 600, headSize, SANS);\n                setSpacing(ctx, -0.035 * headSize);\n                headLines = wrapLines(ctx, V.headline, Math.min(760 * s, inner));\n                setSpacing(ctx, 0);\n                setFont(ctx, 400, bodySize, SANS);\n                bodyLines = wrapLines(ctx, V.body, Math.min(640 * s, inner));\n                total = 36 * s + 18 * s + headLines.length * headSize * 1.02 + 28 * s + bodyLines.length * bodySize * 1.4 + 56 * s + 3 * 40 * s;\n                if (total <= H * 0.94) break;\n                s *= H * 0.94 / total;\n              }\n              var y = (H - total) / 2;\n              ctx.fillStyle = \"#8a7f6b\";\n              fitFont(ctx, V.kicker, inner, 500, 30 * s, SANS);\n              ctx.fillText(V.kicker, pad, y + 18 * s);\n              y += 36 * s + 18 * s;\n              ctx.fillStyle = \"#171410\";\n              setFont(ctx, 600, headSize, SANS);\n              setSpacing(ctx, -0.035 * headSize);\n              headLines.forEach(function (text, i) { ctx.fillText(text, pad, y + (i + 0.5) * headSize * 1.02); });\n              setSpacing(ctx, 0);\n              y += headLines.length * headSize * 1.02 + 28 * s;\n              ctx.fillStyle = \"#5c5346\";\n              setFont(ctx, 400, bodySize, SANS);\n              bodyLines.forEach(function (text, i) { ctx.fillText(text, pad, y + (i + 0.5) * bodySize * 1.4); });\n              y += bodyLines.length * bodySize * 1.4 + 56 * s;\n              [[\"#1f7a72\", 0.92], [\"#e2673a\", 0.68], [\"#2c3f8f\", 0.44]].forEach(function (bar, i) {\n                ctx.fillStyle = bar[0];\n                ctx.fillRect(pad, y + i * 40 * s, inner * bar[1], 26 * s);\n              });\n            }\n\n            function drawScenes() {\n              drawPoster(sceneCanvases[0]);\n            }\n\n            var VERTEX = [\n              \"#version 300 es\",\n              \"in vec2 a_pos;\",\n              \"out vec2 v_uv;\",\n              \"void main() {\",\n              \"  v_uv = vec2(a_pos.x * 0.5 + 0.5, 0.5 - a_pos.y * 0.5);\",\n              \"  gl_Position = vec4(a_pos, 0.0, 1.0);\",\n              \"}\"\n            ].join(\"\\n\");\n            var FRAGMENT = `#version 300 es\nprecision highp float;\n\nuniform sampler2D u_scene;\nuniform float u_aspect;\nuniform float u_cell;\nuniform float u_angle;\nuniform float u_shift;\nuniform vec3 u_paper;\n\nin vec2 v_uv;\nout vec4 outColor;\n\nconst vec3 CYAN_ABSORB = vec3(0.92, 0.12, 0.02);\nconst vec3 MAGENTA_ABSORB = vec3(0.10, 0.88, 0.06);\nconst vec3 YELLOW_ABSORB = vec3(0.03, 0.10, 0.90);\n\nvec2 toSquare(vec2 uv) {\n  return vec2(uv.x * u_aspect, uv.y);\n}\n\nvec2 fromSquare(vec2 p) {\n  return vec2(p.x / u_aspect, p.y);\n}\n\nfloat screenInk(float angle, vec2 drift, vec3 pick) {\n  vec2 p = toSquare(v_uv);\n  float s = sin(angle);\n  float c = cos(angle);\n  vec2 r = vec2(p.x * c - p.y * s, p.x * s + p.y * c);\n\n  vec2 center = (floor(r / u_cell) + 0.5) * u_cell;\n  vec2 unrotated =\n    vec2(center.x * c + center.y * s, -center.x * s + center.y * c);\n\n  vec4 texel = texture(u_scene, fromSquare(unrotated + drift));\n  vec3 straight = texel.rgb / max(texel.a, 0.004);\n  float ink = clamp(1.0 - dot(straight, pick), 0.0, 1.0) * texel.a;\n\n  float radius = sqrt(ink) * u_cell * 0.72;\n  float aa = u_cell * 0.045;\n  float coverage = 1.0 - smoothstep(radius - aa, radius + aa, length(r - center));\n  return coverage * step(0.002, ink);\n}\n\nvoid main() {\n  vec4 source = texture(u_scene, v_uv);\n\n  float cyan =\n    screenInk(u_angle + 0.2618, u_shift * vec2(1.0, 0.0), vec3(1.0, 0.0, 0.0));\n  float magenta =\n    screenInk(u_angle + 1.3090, u_shift * vec2(-0.5, 0.866), vec3(0.0, 1.0, 0.0));\n  float yellow =\n    screenInk(u_angle, u_shift * vec2(-0.5, -0.866), vec3(0.0, 0.0, 1.0));\n\n  vec3 color = u_paper;\n  color *= 1.0 - cyan * CYAN_ABSORB;\n  color *= 1.0 - magenta * MAGENTA_ABSORB;\n  color *= 1.0 - yellow * YELLOW_ABSORB;\n\n  outColor = vec4(color * source.a, source.a);\n}`;\n\n            canvas.width = cw;\n            canvas.height = ch;\n            var gl = canvas.getContext(\"webgl2\", { antialias: false, depth: false, stencil: false, preserveDrawingBuffer: true });\n            function compile(type, source) {\n              var shader = gl.createShader(type);\n              gl.shaderSource(shader, source);\n              gl.compileShader(shader);\n              if (!gl.getShaderParameter(shader, gl.COMPILE_STATUS)) throw new Error(gl.getShaderInfoLog(shader) || \"shader compile failed\");\n              return shader;\n            }\n            var paint = null;\n            var upload = function () {};\n            var extraUpload = function () {};\n            var frameFn = function () {};\n            var texUnits = [];\n            try {\n              if (!gl) throw new Error(\"WebGL2 is not available\");\n              var program = gl.createProgram();\n              gl.attachShader(program, compile(gl.VERTEX_SHADER, VERTEX));\n              gl.attachShader(program, compile(gl.FRAGMENT_SHADER, FRAGMENT));\n              gl.linkProgram(program);\n              if (!gl.getProgramParameter(program, gl.LINK_STATUS)) throw new Error(gl.getProgramInfoLog(program) || \"link failed\");\n              gl.useProgram(program);\n              var buffer = gl.createBuffer();\n              gl.bindBuffer(gl.ARRAY_BUFFER, buffer);\n              gl.bufferData(gl.ARRAY_BUFFER, new Float32Array([-1, -1, 1, -1, -1, 1, 1, 1]), gl.STATIC_DRAW);\n              var aPos = gl.getAttribLocation(program, \"a_pos\");\n              gl.enableVertexAttribArray(aPos);\n              gl.vertexAttribPointer(aPos, 2, gl.FLOAT, false, 0, 0);\n              function makeTexture(unit) {\n                var texture = gl.createTexture();\n                gl.activeTexture(gl.TEXTURE0 + unit);\n                gl.bindTexture(gl.TEXTURE_2D, texture);\n                gl.texParameteri(gl.TEXTURE_2D, gl.TEXTURE_WRAP_S, gl.CLAMP_TO_EDGE);\n                gl.texParameteri(gl.TEXTURE_2D, gl.TEXTURE_WRAP_T, gl.CLAMP_TO_EDGE);\n                gl.texParameteri(gl.TEXTURE_2D, gl.TEXTURE_MIN_FILTER, gl.LINEAR);\n                gl.texParameteri(gl.TEXTURE_2D, gl.TEXTURE_MAG_FILTER, gl.LINEAR);\n                return texture;\n              }\n              gl.viewport(0, 0, cw, ch);\n              function u(name) { return gl.getUniformLocation(program, name); }\n              [\"u_scene\"].forEach(function (name, unit) {\n                makeTexture(unit);\n                gl.uniform1i(u(name), unit);\n              });\n              gl.uniform1f(u(\"u_aspect\"), W / H);\n              var frameLoc = u(\"u_frame\");\n              var timeLoc = u(\"u_time\");\n              upload = function () {\n                sceneCanvases.forEach(function (el, unit) {\n                  gl.activeTexture(gl.TEXTURE0 + unit);\n                  gl.texImage2D(gl.TEXTURE_2D, 0, gl.RGBA, gl.RGBA, gl.UNSIGNED_BYTE, el);\n                });\n                extraUpload();\n              };\n\n              gl.uniform1f(u(\"u_cell\"), Math.max(V.dot_size * S, 1) / H);\n              gl.uniform1f(u(\"u_angle\"), V.angle * Math.PI / 180);\n              gl.uniform1f(u(\"u_shift\"), V.misregistration * S / H);\n              var paper = rgb(V.paper_tint);\n              gl.uniform3f(u(\"u_paper\"), paper[0], paper[1], paper[2]);\n\n              paint = function (frame) {\n                gl.uniform1f(frameLoc, frame);\n                gl.uniform1f(timeLoc, frame / 30);\n                frameFn(frame, frame / 30);\n                gl.clearColor(0, 0, 0, 0);\n                gl.clear(gl.COLOR_BUFFER_BIT);\n                gl.drawArrays(gl.TRIANGLE_STRIP, 0, 4);\n              };\n            } catch (err) {\n              stage.classList.add(\"htp-off\");\n              if (window.console) console.warn(NAME + \":\", err.message);\n            }\n\n            // The scenes are redrawn whenever a web font finishes loading, so no frame keeps a fallback face.\n            var fontEpoch = 0;\n            var sceneEpoch = -1;\n            var lastFrame = 0;\n            function render(frame) {\n              lastFrame = frame;\n              if (sceneEpoch !== fontEpoch) {\n                sceneEpoch = fontEpoch;\n                drawScenes();\n                upload();\n              }\n              if (paint) paint(frame);\n            }\n            if (document.fonts && document.fonts.load) {\n              [\"400 34px Geist\", \"500 30px Geist\", \"600 44px Geist\", \"400 44px 'Geist Mono'\"].forEach(function (face) {\n                document.fonts.load(face).then(function () { fontEpoch++; render(lastFrame); }, function () {});\n              });\n            }\n\n            var total = parseFloat(root.dataset.duration || \"3\");\n            var totalFrames = Math.round(total * 30);\n            var clock = { frame: 0 };\n            var tl = gsap.timeline({ paused: true });\n            tl.to(clock, {\n              frame: totalFrames,\n              duration: total,\n              ease: \"none\",\n              onUpdate: function () { render(Math.round(clock.frame)); }\n            }, 0);\n            render(0);\n            tl.seek(0);\n            window.__timelines = window.__timelines || {};\n            window.__timelines[NAME] = tl;\n          })();\n        </script>\n      </div>\n    </template>\n  </body>\n</html>\n"
  }
 ],
